---
import evidence from "../../../skill-evals/jev-capability-advisor/benchmarks/next-skill-2026-09-24.json";
import { nextSkillComparison } from "../lib/jev-next-skill-benchmarks.mjs";
import { repoUrl } from "../lib/skills";

interface Props { comparison?: ReturnType<typeof nextSkillComparison>; }
const { comparison = nextSkillComparison(evidence) } = Astro.props;
const number = (value: number) => value.toLocaleString("en-US", { maximumFractionDigits: 1 });
const seconds = (milliseconds: number) => (milliseconds / 1000).toFixed(3);
---

<section class="jev-next" id="benchmarks" aria-labelledby="jev-next-title">
  <header class="jev-next__header">
    <div>
      <p class="jev-next__eyebrow">Explicit next-skill profile · measured input savings</p>
      <h2 id="jev-next-title">One next skill.<br />Less model input.</h2>
      <p>Fewer provider input tokens than both measured Hussi variants, with every skill and no-match case correct in these two cohorts.</p>
    </div>
    <a class="jev-next__source" href={repoUrl(comparison.readmePath)}>Read the benchmark details <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
  </header>
  <p class="jev-next__context"><code>next_skill</code><span>{comparison.catalogRecords}-entry skill catalog</span><span>{comparison.model}</span></p>

  <div class="jev-next__cohorts">
    {comparison.cohorts.map((cohort) => (
      <section class="jev-next__cohort" aria-labelledby={`${cohort.id}-title`}>
        <div class="jev-next__cohort-heading">
          <h3 id={`${cohort.id}-title`}>{cohort.label}</h3>
          <p>{cohort.date} · {cohort.skillObservations} skill choices + {cohort.noneObservations} no-match observations</p>
        </div>
        <dl class="jev-next__metrics">
          <div><dt>Less total skill-selection input<br /><strong>vs published Hussi9</strong></dt><dd>{cohort.reductionVsPublished.toFixed(1)}<span>%</span></dd></div>
          <div><dt>Less total skill-selection input<br /><strong>vs our pooled Hussi9 control</strong></dt><dd>{cohort.reductionVsControl.toFixed(1)}<span>%</span></dd></div>
        </dl>
        <div class="jev-next__table-scroll" role="region" aria-label={`${cohort.label}: input tokens and selection quality`} tabindex="0">
          <table>
            <caption>Skill-selection input · lower is better</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Variant</th><th scope="col">Median input<br /><span>Total below</span></th><th scope="col">Skills<br />correct</th><th scope="col">No match<br />correct</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{cohort.rows.map((row) => (
              <tr class:list={{ "jev-next__winner": row.highlight }}>
                <th scope="row">{row.label}{row.experiment && <small>Our experiment</small>}</th>
                <td><strong>{number(row.medianInputTokens)}</strong><small>{number(row.totalInputTokens)} total</small></td>
                <td>{row.skillCorrect}/{row.skillObservations}</td>
                <td>{row.noneCorrect}/{row.noneObservations}</td>
              </tr>
            ))}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="jev-next__timing"><strong>Selection time, separately:</strong> ours {seconds(cohort.rows[0].medianLatencyMs)} s; published Hussi9 {seconds(cohort.rows[1].medianLatencyMs)} s; pooled control {seconds(cohort.rows[2].medianLatencyMs)} s. Medians.{cohort.pooledControlFaster && <> <strong>The pooled control was faster here.</strong></>}</p>
        <details class="jev-next__none">
          <summary>No-match input, reported separately</summary>
          <ul>{cohort.rows.map((row) => <li><strong>{row.label}:</strong> {number(row.noneMedianInputTokens)} median input tokens; {number(row.noneTotalInputTokens)} total.</li>)}</ul>
        </details>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <ul class="jev-next__why" aria-label="How the next-skill profile works">
    <li><strong>One explicit choice.</strong> Ask which skill to load next. One choice question and at most one provider call; additional work remains unassessed.</li>
    <li><strong>A compact catalog.</strong> Shared context and compact card encoding reduce repeated text. Candidate limits and activation restrictions remain visible.</li>
    <li><strong>The full default stays available.</strong> Use <code>general</code> for skills, tools and compound recommendations. The host explicitly chooses the narrower profile.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="jev-next__scope">Percentages compare <strong>total provider input tokens</strong> across all skill-choice observations; medians are shown separately. Every dispatched call counts. The cohorts use the same catalog and model and are not pooled. This measures next-skill selection input, not whole-agent tokens, price, skill-loading time or complete-task speed.</p>
  <details class="jev-next__details">
    <summary>Method, limits and unchanged general behavior</summary>
    <p>The matched cohort contains 48 tasks and the confirmation cohort 32, each repeated twice for three variants: {comparison.confirmationExecutions} observations. A separate {comparison.developmentExecutions}-observation development smoke is retained in the report. Confirmation uses independently authored synthetic tasks; their author knew earlier diagnostic themes. This is observed accuracy on these tasks, not a guarantee for future requests.</p>
    <p>All scheduled outcomes and provider-reported input remain accounted for, including incorrect comparison results. The input gate requires both lower median and lower total input against both Hussi variants, for skill choices and for each full cohort including no-match cases. Each comparison retains its original thresholds and timing behavior. Selection timing excludes process startup, skill loading and task execution.</p>
    <p>Hussi9 means its pinned published Jev chooser, not its full router, hooks or fallback workflow. The pooled HTTPS control is our modification, not a published Hussi9 release. Both it and our session retain a process and connection. No universal speed ranking or new Native comparison is claimed.</p>
    <p>The default general path has separate deterministic evidence: {comparison.parity.replays} recorded-response replays preserve {comparison.parity.preservedWrong} incorrect baseline outcomes, including {comparison.parity.preservedErrors} errors. Replay checks equal behavior for equal supplied responses; it is not a new live accuracy measurement. Earlier failed optimization attempts remain in the linked evaluation record.</p>
    {comparison.knownInheritedLimitation && <p><strong>Retained limitation:</strong> {comparison.knownInheritedLimitation}</p>}
  </details>
  <footer class="jev-next__footer">
    <a href={repoUrl(comparison.evidencePath)}>Audited two-cohort results</a>
    <a href={comparison.hussiSource}>Pinned Hussi9 source</a>
    <a href="#selection-speed">Historical general-profile speed comparison</a>
  </footer>
</section>

<style>
  .jev-next { margin-top: 1.25rem; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2.5rem); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface-solid); color: var(--foreground); scroll-margin-top: 7rem; }
  .jev-next p, .jev-next li { line-height: 1.6; }
  .jev-next__header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .jev-next__eyebrow { margin: 0 0 .6rem; color: var(--secondary); font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .jev-next h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2rem, 4.5vw, 3.4rem); line-height: 1.1; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .jev-next__header p:last-child { max-width: 58ch; margin: 1rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; }
  .jev-next__source { max-width: 18ch; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .jev-next__context { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .5rem 1rem; align-items: center; margin: 1.15rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .72rem; }
  .jev-next__context span { padding-left: 1rem; border-left: 1px solid var(--border-strong); }
  .jev-next__cohorts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.2rem; margin-top: 1.6rem; }
  .jev-next__cohort { min-width: 0; padding: 1.2rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface-muted); }
  .jev-next h3 { margin: 0; font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.4; }
  .jev-next__cohort-heading > p { margin: .3rem 0 0; font-size: .72rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .jev-next__metrics { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.4rem 0 1rem; }
  .jev-next__metrics > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column-reverse; gap: .55rem; }
  .jev-next__metrics dt { font-size: .67rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  .jev-next__metrics dt strong { color: var(--foreground); font-weight: 600; }
  .jev-next__metrics dd { margin: 0; color: var(--primary); font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4.5vw, 3.5rem); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -.055em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .jev-next__metrics > div + div dd { color: var(--secondary); }
  .jev-next__metrics dd span { font-size: .5em; margin-left: .08em; }
  .jev-next__table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .jev-next table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; font-size: .72rem; }
  .jev-next caption { padding-block: .6rem; text-align: left; font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .jev-next th, .jev-next td { padding: .7rem .35rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: middle; }
  .jev-next thead th { font-size: .66rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
  .jev-next thead th span { font-weight: 400; }
  .jev-next tbody th { min-width: 7rem; font-weight: 550; line-height: 1.4; }
  .jev-next tbody td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .jev-next table small { display: block; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .25rem; font-size: .62rem; font-weight: 400; }
  .jev-next__winner th, .jev-next__winner td { color: var(--primary); font-weight: 750; }
  .jev-next__timing { margin: .9rem 0 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: .68rem; }
  .jev-next__timing strong { font-weight: 600; }
  .jev-next__none { font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .jev-next summary { cursor: pointer; padding-block: .85rem; font-weight: 600; }
  .jev-next details ul { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin: 0 0 .8rem; }
  .jev-next details li + li { margin-top: .3rem; }
  .jev-next__why { list-style: none; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.3rem; padding: 1.6rem 0; margin: 1.5rem 0 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; }
  .jev-next__why strong { display: block; margin-bottom: .3rem; color: var(--foreground); }
  .jev-next__scope { margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .74rem; }
  .jev-next__details { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: .76rem; }
  .jev-next__details summary { color: var(--foreground); }
  .jev-next__footer { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .6rem 1.2rem; padding-top: .6rem; font-size: .73rem; }
  .jev-next a:focus-visible, .jev-next summary:focus-visible, .jev-next__table-scroll:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--primary); outline-offset: 4px; border-radius: 3px; }
  @media (max-width: 1050px) { .jev-next__cohorts { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .jev-next__header { flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem; }
    .jev-next__source { max-width: none; }
    .jev-next__cohort { padding: .9rem; }
    .jev-next__why { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: .9rem; }
    .jev-next__metrics dd { font-size: 2.8rem; }
  }
</style>
